{
  "Project A": {
    "Pros": [
      "• Clarity of value proposition: Strong focus on addressing the urgent need for AI skill development through accessible, guided learning.\n• Market size and demand: Targets the large and growing market for AI education across individuals, creators, and enterprises.\n• Revenue model and sustainability: Multiple revenue streams from learners, creators (course monetization), and enterprise programs.\n• Differentiation: Combines AI mentor, agent playground, and creator tools into a social learning ecosystem, distinguishing from standard online courses.\n• Impact and evidence plan: Clear plan for global challenges and certifications, with emphasis on human-centered design and ethical AI.\n• Risk awareness and mitigation: Acknowledges technical and UX risks, with mitigations like partnerships and monthly updates.",
      "• Feasibility and development plan: Builds on an existing platform foundation, with a phased roadmap extending to September 2026."
    ],
    "Cons": [
      "• Feasibility and development plan: Timeline is long (prototype in Feb 2026), raising questions about execution speed and market timing.\n• Risk awareness and mitigation: Risks are broadly stated (e.g., 'integrating secure, scalable AI systems') without detailed technical mitigations.\n• Differentiation: While features are innovative, the AI education space is crowded; success hinges on execution quality.\n• Evidence plan: Relies on stated existing foundation but lacks quantified traction or user metrics."
    ]
  },
  "Project B": {
    "Pros": [
      "• Clarity of value proposition: Clear and specific—replaces mouse with a wearable ring to reduce strain and improve efficiency.\n• Market size and demand: Addresses universal computer users across office, creative, and gaming segments.\n• Feasibility and development plan: Detailed, time-bound roadmap with specific engineering milestones (EVT, DVT, PVT) and near-term delivery (shipment Dec 2025).\n• Differentiation: Unique hardware-software combo with 40+ gestures, cross-platform compatibility, and no-driver Bluetooth HID.\n• Revenue model and sustainability: Hardware sales with optional software upsell (Pro license), supported by clear product roadmap.\n• Risk awareness and mitigation: Identifies concrete manufacturing and Bluetooth risks, with experienced production partners as mitigation.\n• Impact and evidence plan: Strong technical specifications (e.g., capacitive touch resolution), compliance targets (CE/FCC), and environmental durability focus."
    ],
    "Cons": [
      "• Market size and demand: While broad, wearable input devices face adoption hurdles versus entrenched peripherals like mice.\n• Revenue model and sustainability: Dependent on hardware sales; recurring revenue limited to optional software upgrades.\n• Risk awareness and mitigation: Manufacturing scaling risks remain high despite partner experience.\n• Differentiation: Competitors exist in gesture control (e.g., smart rings, motion controllers); success depends on flawless UX and gesture accuracy."
    ]
  }
}

